    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i'm taking the eurostar from st pancras to paris next week. i have a couple of really heavy suitcases and i'm a bit worried about the check-in process and the bag limits. what are the actual rules for luggage and how early do i really need to be there to get through everything without a massive headache?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Eurostar allows each passenger two heavy bags and one shoulder bag, but they prioritize checking hand luggage first at Manchester and Lyon. Each heavy bag should not exceed 32kg (70lbs), including handling charges. Check-ins start at 510 AM from London to Paris and it’s advisable to arrive at least 2-3 hours before departure. You can report lost bags directly through a form and are due a refund if it isn't found. It’s always best to arrive early for new passengers during peak travel times.",
